[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[b]Installer[/b] — download the setup .exe and run it. It creates a Start-menu shortcut and sets up the WebView2 runtime if your Windows doesn't already have it.
[b]Portable[/b] — download the portable .zip, unzip it anywhere, and double-click Palbox Studio.exe. Nothing to install; keep the folder together.
[b]With Vortex[/b] — the portable folder doubles as a Vortex tool: on the Palworld dashboard, [b]+ Add Tool -> New...[/b], point [b]Target[/b] at Palbox Studio.exe.

[b][color=#e0b050]Safety first:[/color][/b] Palbox Studio never edits a live save in place without first taking a verified backup. Close Palworld completely before saving edits. Your box lives at %LOCALAPPDATA%\Pal\Saved\SaveGames\<your-id>\GlobalPalStorage.sav.

[i]Windows 11 already includes the WebView2 runtime Palbox Studio uses. On older Windows, if it won't start, install the free Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime and try again.[/i]

